  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Oblonganoside C to Caov-4, which is targeted by K-252a, a known inhibitor of MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4. The second pathway connects Oblonganoside C to Serine/threonine-protein kinase SBK1, which is targeted by benzocaine, another compound that influences the same kinase. The third pathway reveals a more complex interaction, where Oblonganoside C targets Tyrosine-protein kinase Fes/Fps, which in turn targets a complex compound that ultimately affects the same kinase. These findings suggest that Oblonganoside C may modulate MAP/microtubule affinity-regulating kinase 4 through distinct but related mechanisms, potentially involving kinase inhibition or regulation through downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a role for Oblonganoside C in influencing the activity of this kinase, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
